# /etc/pf.anchors/netforge on Mac 3 (Backend A), Phase 2 Extension C
# Only the nginx edge (Mac 2, 10.7.17.248) may open TCP connections to Backend A on port 3001.
# pf evaluates "quick" rules top-down and stops at the first match:
#   1. traffic from the edge -> pass
#   2. anyone else            -> silently dropped (the client sees a timeout, not "refused")
# Nothing else (Wi-Fi, DHCP, DNS, ping, the standby nginx on 8443) is matched, so connectivity is unaffected.
pass in quick on en0 proto tcp from 10.7.17.248 to 10.7.28.81 port 3001
block drop in quick on en0 proto tcp from any to 10.7.28.81 port 3001
